        "detail": "船帆建筑 · 运河水街午餐",
        "art_english": "The Grand Canal Museum of Beijing in Tongzhou: a contemporary cultural complex with TWO distinct broad low structures separated by a pedestrian WATER STREET. The shared entrance hall roof has an upturned canal-BOAT-inspired profile, and the exhibition main building has a raised SAIL-inspired roof. Silver-gray metal roof surfaces, pale masonry and glass, deep shaded openings and a dock-like landscaped water lane between the structures. Three-quarter elevated view clearly distinguishes both roof forms and water-street relationship, with gold and flame-orange autumn trees. This is the Tongzhou canal museum, not the Capital Museum in central Beijing, not a literal sailing ship on water, not one generic rectangle.",
