        "art_english": "Beijing Performing Arts Centre, Tongzhou: THREE distinct silvery-white theater volumes in a group, each with a single-ridge double-pitched GABLED roof inspired by the historical canal granaries. The broad faces are clad in shimmering fine perforated aluminum screens; the soft draped folds and raised side contours evoke sails and theater curtains parting. Wide low civic plazas and glass bases, three complementary sculptural granary silhouettes visible together, autumn trees and deep vivid blue shadows. Not smooth egg-shaped domes, not the central Beijing National Centre for Performing Arts, no needle towers, no generic skyscrapers.",
