          "detail": "银杏穹顶 · 玻璃森林书苑",
          "art_english": "Beijing City Library in Tongzhou, an original architecturally detailed exterior three-quarter illustration: a broad low rectangular glass building with transparent floor-to-ceiling structural glass walls, generous flat roof overhang, tall slender white columns inside that mushroom into overlapping GINKGO-LEAF-shaped ceiling panels. The sculpted stepped terraced reading landscape is visible through the glass. Sunlight and orange-gold trees at the entrance. Keep the low horizontal transparent envelope and canopy of flat fan-shaped ginkgo leaves; not a domed old library or a forest growing through books. No readable signage.",
